4. Formal Specification in Lean 4

4.1 Vertices and edges

```lean
import Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic
import Mathlib.Data.List.Basic

namespace TLSACE.v0_5

inductive TLSACEVertex
  | C   -- Cognitive Capability
  | O   -- Objectives / Alignment
  | G   -- Governance Intensity
  | R   -- Resource Budget
  | E   -- Environment Constraints
  | Ad  -- Granted Autonomy
  | Aex -- Exercised Autonomy (Collider and Mediator)
  | B   -- Exploration Behavior
  | H   -- Multidimensional Cooperation
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

open TLSACEVertex

def DirectedEdge : TLSACEVertex → TLSACEVertex → Prop
  | G,   Ad  => True
  | Ad,  Aex => True
  | C,   Aex => True
  | R,   Aex => True
  | C,   B   => True
  | O,   B   => True
  | G,   B   => True
  | R,   B   => True
  | E,   B   => True
  | Aex, B   => True
  | C,   H   => True
  | O,   H   => True
  | G,   H   => True
  | E,   H   => True
  | Aex, H   => True
  | _,   _   => False
```

4.2 Descendant relation

```lean
inductive IsDescendant : TLSACEVertex → TLSACEVertex → Prop
  | direct {u v : TLSACEVertex} (h : DirectedEdge u v) : IsDescendant u v
  | trans {u v w : TLSACEVertex}
      (h1 : IsDescendant u v) (h2 : IsDescendant v w) : IsDescendant u w
```

4.3 Triplet classification

A triplet (u, v, w) along a path is classified according to the orientation of its two edges:

\text{classifyTriplet}(u, v, w) =
\begin{cases}
\text{ChainForward} & \text{if } u \to v \text{ and } v \to w \\
\text{ChainBackward} & \text{if } u \leftarrow v \text{ and } v \leftarrow w \\
\text{Fork} & \text{if } u \leftarrow v \text{ and } v \to w \\
\text{Collider} & \text{if } u \to v \text{ and } v \leftarrow w \\
\text{None} & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}

```lean
inductive TripletType
  | ChainForward
  | ChainBackward
  | Fork
  | Collider
  | None

def classifyTriplet (u v w : TLSACEVertex) : TripletType :=
  if DirectedEdge u v && DirectedEdge v w then TripletType.ChainForward
  else if DirectedEdge v u && DirectedEdge w v then TripletType.ChainBackward
  else if DirectedEdge v u && DirectedEdge v w then TripletType.Fork
  else if DirectedEdge u v && DirectedEdge w v then TripletType.Collider
  else TripletType.None
```

4.4 Path blocking

A path is blocked given a conditioning set Z if at least one triplet along the path is blocked. The blocking rules are:

\text{IsTripletBlocked}(u, v, w, Z) =
\begin{cases}
v \in Z & \text{if ChainForward or ChainBackward or Fork} \\
\neg(v \in Z \text{ or } \exists d \in \text{Desc}(v) : d \in Z) & \text{if Collider} \\
\text{false} & \text{if None}
\end{cases}

```lean
def InZOrDescendantInZ (v : TLSACEVertex) (Z : List TLSACEVertex) : Bool :=
  Z.contains v || (List.any Z (fun z => sorry))

def IsTripletBlocked (u v w : TLSACEVertex) (Z : List TLSACEVertex) : Bool :=
  match classifyTriplet u v w with
  | TripletType.ChainForward  => Z.contains v
  | TripletType.ChainBackward => Z.contains v
  | TripletType.Fork          => Z.contains v
  | TripletType.Collider      => !(InZOrDescendantInZ v Z)
  | TripletType.None          => false
```

```lean
def IsPathBlocked (path : List TLSACEVertex) (Z : List TLSACEVertex) : Bool :=
  match path with
  | []           => true
  | [_]          => true
  | [_, _]       => true
  | u :: v :: w :: rest =>
      if IsTripletBlocked u v w Z then true
      else IsPathBlocked (v :: w :: rest) Z
```

4.5 D-separation

```lean
def DSeparated (X Y Z : List TLSACEVertex)
    (allPaths : List (List TLSACEVertex)) : Prop :=
  ∀ path ∈ allPaths,
    (path.head? = X.head? ∧ path.getLast? = Y.getLast?) →
    IsPathBlocked path Z = true
```

