8. Red-Team Analysis

Adversarial case What it tests Consequence for TLSACE
Highly autonomous, durably cooperative agent Does autonomy necessarily cause rupture? Refutes any deterministic version
Highly capable, non-exploratory agent Does capability suffice for exploration? Supports distinction of capability and objectives
Low-capability rule violator Is performance necessary for violation? Tests role of objectives and control
Cooperation-simulating agent Are indicators robust to manipulation? Requires independent verification, not self-report
Strong governance blocking legitimate experiments Can governance reduce both risk and utility? Requires measuring cost of controls
Agent whose reported objectives differ from operative ones Do stated objectives predict behavior? Requires behavioral verification

A counterexample does not automatically refute a probabilistic hypothesis. It can refute a universal claim or reveal a missing variable.

