  | _,   _   => False
```

Lemma B.1 (Decidability of edges). For all u, v \in V, the proposition \text{DirectedEdge}(u, v) is decidable.

Proof. The definition of DirectedEdge is a pattern match on finite constructors, each returning True or False. Decidability follows by case analysis on the constructor pair. \square

B.4 Acyclicity

The graph is acyclic. Define the rank function:

\rho(C) = 0, \quad \rho(O) = 0, \quad \rho(G) = 0, \quad \rho(R) = 0, \quad \rho(E) = 0

\rho(A_d) = 1, \quad \rho(A_{\mathrm{ex}}) = 2, \quad \rho(B) = 3, \quad \rho(H) = 3

Lemma B.2 (Rank monotonicity). For every directed edge u \to v, \rho(u) < \rho(v).

Proof. Case analysis on the edge relation:

\begin{aligned}
G \to A_d &: \rho(G) = 0 < 1 = \rho(A_d) \\
A_d \to A_{\mathrm{ex}} &: \rho(A_d) = 1 < 2 = \rho(A_{\mathrm{ex}}) \\
C \to A_{\mathrm{ex}} &: \rho(C) = 0 < 2 = \rho(A_{\mathrm{ex}}) \\
R \to A_{\mathrm{ex}} &: \rho(R) = 0 < 2 = \rho(A_{\mathrm{ex}}) \\
C \to B &: \rho(C) = 0 < 3 = \rho(B) \\
&\vdots \\
A_{\mathrm{ex}} \to H &: \rho(A_{\mathrm{ex}}) = 2 < 3 = \rho(H)
\end{aligned}

Every edge strictly increases rank. \square

Theorem B.3 (Acyclicity). The TLSACE graph contains no directed cycle.

Proof. Suppose there exists a directed cycle v_1 \to v_2 \to \cdots \to v_k \to v_1. By Lemma B.2, \rho(v_1) < \rho(v_2) < \cdots < \rho(v_k) < \rho(v_1), a contradiction. \square

B.5 Descendants

```lean
inductive IsDescendant : TLSACEVertex → TLSACEVertex → Prop
  | direct {u v : TLSACEVertex} (h : DirectedEdge u v) : IsDescendant u v
  | trans {u v w : TLSACEVertex}
      (h1 : IsDescendant u v) (h2 : IsDescendant v w) : IsDescendant u w
```

Lemma B.4 (Descendant computation terminates). For every v \in V, the set \text{Desc}(v) is finite and computable.

Proof. The vertex set V has cardinality 9. The relation \text{IsDescendant} is well-founded by the rank function of Lemma B.2. Computing \text{Desc}(v) proceeds by iterating over the finite edge set, at most 9^2 = 81 iterations. \square

B.6 Triplet classification

```lean
inductive TripletType
  | ChainForward
  | ChainBackward
  | Fork
  | Collider
  | None

def classifyTriplet (u v w : TLSACEVertex) : TripletType :=
  if DirectedEdge u v && DirectedEdge v w then TripletType.ChainForward
  else if DirectedEdge v u && DirectedEdge w v then TripletType.ChainBackward
  else if DirectedEdge v u && DirectedEdge v w then TripletType.Fork
  else if DirectedEdge u v && DirectedEdge w v then TripletType.Collider
  else TripletType.None
```

Lemma B.5 (Classification exhaustiveness). For all u, v, w \in V, \text{classifyTriplet}(u, v, w) returns exactly one of the five constructors, and the classification is exhaustive over all possible edge orientations.

Proof. The four conditional branches cover all combinations where at least one edge exists between consecutive vertices. The None case covers all remaining configurations. \square

B.7 Path blocking

```lean
def InZOrDescendantInZ (v : TLSACEVertex) (Z : List TLSACEVertex) : Bool :=
  Z.contains v ||
    (List.any Z (fun z =>
      match z, v with
      | _, _ => decide (IsDescendant v z)))

def IsTripletBlocked (u v w : TLSACEVertex) (Z : List TLSACEVertex) : Bool :=
  match classifyTriplet u v w with
  | TripletType.ChainForward  => Z.contains v
  | TripletType.ChainBackward => Z.contains v
  | TripletType.Fork          => Z.contains v
  | TripletType.Collider      => !(InZOrDescendantInZ v Z)
  | TripletType.None          => false

def IsPathBlocked (path : List TLSACEVertex) (Z : List TLSACEVertex) : Bool :=
  match path with
  | []           => true
  | [_]          => true
  | [_, _]       => true
  | u :: v :: w :: rest =>
      if IsTripletBlocked u v w Z then true
      else IsPathBlocked (v :: w :: rest) Z
```

Lemma B.6 (Path blocking termination). For every finite path \pi and conditioning set Z, \text{IsPathBlocked}(\pi, Z) terminates.

Proof. The recursive call reduces the path length by one at each step. The base cases of length 0, 1, and 2 terminate immediately. \square

B.8 D-separation

```lean
def DSeparated (X Y Z : List TLSACEVertex)
    (allPaths : List (List TLSACEVertex)) : Prop :=
  ∀ path ∈ allPaths,
    (path.head? = X.head? ∧ path.getLast? = Y.getLast?) →
    IsPathBlocked path Z = true

def DConnected (X Y Z : List TLSACEVertex)
    (allPaths : List (List TLSACEVertex)) : Prop :=
  ¬ DSeparated X Y Z allPaths
```

