Appendix D. Full Proof of Theorem 2: Backdoor Adjustment

Theorem 2 (Backdoor adjustment with \{G, O, E\}). Let Z_{\text{bd}} = [G, O, E]. Then

\text{IsPathBlocked}([C, A_{\mathrm{ex}}, A_d, G, H], [G, O, E]) = \text{true}

Lemma D.1 (Collider at A_{\mathrm{ex}} is closed). With Z = [G, O, E],

\text{IsTripletBlocked}(C, A_{\mathrm{ex}}, A_d, [G, O, E]) = \text{true}

Proof. By Lemma C.1, the triplet is a collider. We compute \text{InZOrDescendantInZ}(A_{\mathrm{ex}}, [G, O, E]). Since A_{\mathrm{ex}} \notin \{G, O, E\}, the first disjunct is False. Since no element of \{G, O, E\} is a descendant of A_{\mathrm{ex}} (indeed, A_{\mathrm{ex}} has descendants B and H, neither of which is in Z), the second disjunct is False. Hence \text{InZOrDescendantInZ}(A_{\mathrm{ex}}, [G, O, E]) = \text{false}, and

\text{IsTripletBlocked}(C, A_{\mathrm{ex}}, A_d, [G, O, E]) = \neg \text{false} = \text{true}

\square

Proof of Theorem 2. By the definition of IsPathBlocked, the path is blocked at the first triplet by Lemma D.1. Hence

\text{IsPathBlocked}([C, A_{\mathrm{ex}}, A_d, G, H], [G, O, E]) = \text{true}

\square

Lemma D.2 (Fork at G provides an additional blocking mechanism). The triplet (A_d, G, H) is a fork at G, and G \in Z_{\text{bd}}, so it is blocked.

Proof. We verify \text{DirectedEdge}(G, A_d) = \text{True} and \text{DirectedEdge}(G, H) = \text{True}. The third branch of classifyTriplet checks \text{DirectedEdge}(G, A_d) \wedge \text{DirectedEdge}(G, H) = \text{True}, so the classification is Fork. Since G \in [G, O, E], we have

\text{IsTripletBlocked}(A_d, G, H, [G, O, E]) = Z.contains(G) = \text{true}

\square

Corollary D.3 (Backdoor criterion satisfied). The set \{G, O, E\} satisfies the backdoor criterion for estimating the total effect of C on H.

Proof. The set \{G, O, E\} contains no descendant of C, since C's descendants are A_{\mathrm{ex}}, B, H, and none of these is in \{G, O, E\}. By Theorem 2 and Lemma D.2, all non-causal paths between C and H through \{G, O, E\} are blocked. Hence the backdoor criterion is satisfied. \square

