Appendix J. Statistical Model Specifications

J.1 Total effects on exploration behavior

B_{ij} = \beta_0 + \beta_C C_i + \beta_O O_j + \beta_G G_j + \beta_R R_j + \beta_{CO} C_i O_j + \beta_{CG} C_i G_j + u_i + \varepsilon_{ij}

where:

· i indexes agent instances (or model seeds),
· j indexes experimental conditions,
· u_i \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma_u^2) is a random effect for agent instance,
· \varepsilon_{ij} \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma_\varepsilon^2) is the residual error,
· interactions \beta_{CO}, \beta_{CG} are preregistered.

J.2 Total effects on cooperation dimensions

For each k \in \{c, r, s, k, f, d\}:

H_{k,ij} = \gamma_{0k} + \gamma_{Ck} C_i + \gamma_{Ok} O_j + \gamma_{Gk} G_j + \gamma_{COk} C_i O_j + \gamma_{CGk} C_i G_j + v_i + \varepsilon_{k,ij}

J.3 Mediation model

Secondary analysis, explicitly labeled as mediation:

H_{k,ij} = \gamma_{0k} + \gamma_{Ck} C_i + \gamma_{Ok} O_j + \gamma_{Gk} G_j + \gamma_{Ak} A_{\mathrm{ex},ij} + v_i + \varepsilon_{k,ij}

The coefficient \gamma_{Ak} is not interpreted as a causal effect without direct manipulation of A_{\mathrm{ex}}. Sequential ignorability is assumed and stated.

J.4 Critical violations model

\Pr(V_{ij} = 1) = \mathrm{logit}^{-1}\!\left(\delta_0 + \delta_C C_i + \delta_O O_j + \delta_G G_j + \delta_{CG} C_i G_j\right)

with severity-weighted counts analyzed via negative binomial regression where appropriate.

J.5 Multiple comparison correction

Holm–Bonferroni or Benjamini–Hochberg correction is preregistered. The test family comprises:

· Six cooperation dimensions,
· Two preregistered interactions,
· One exploration behavior outcome.

Total: nine tests in the primary family.

J.6 Power analysis

Power is simulated under effect sizes justified by a pilot or the literature. Target: 1 - \beta \geq 0.80 for the smallest theoretically important effect. N is not fixed after observing results.

J.7 Model comparison

· M0: B \sim C, H_k \sim C
· M1: B \sim C + O, H_k \sim C + O
· M2: B \sim C + O + G, H_k \sim C + O + G
· M3: Full model including R, E, A_{\mathrm{ex}}, and interactions

Criteria: out-of-sample predictive performance, calibration, and explanation of critical outcomes. M3 is justified only if it improves over M2 on at least two of the three criteria.

